@title Class 9B, Monday: three timetable looks
@subtitle Same day, three treatments, shown as it stands at 11:30

All three looks below show the same real day, Monday for class 9B, and each marks what is happening at 11:30: Break ended at 11:10, so P3 Science in Lab 2 with Dr Banerjee is on.

! The page compiler sets colour and type, so these looks differ in layout and emphasis. School navy and amber, subject colours and display fonts are not applied here.

## Look 1: station departures board

Every period on one dense grid, one row each, with a status column like a departures board.

table = Time,Period,Subject,Room,Teacher,Note,Status; 08:50,P1,Maths,Rm 12,Mr Osei,-,Done; 09:50,P2,English,Rm 4,Ms Lindqvist,-,Done; 10:50-11:10,Break,-,-,-,-,Done; 11:10,P3,Science,Lab 2,Dr Banerjee,Bring goggles,In progress; 12:10,P4,PE,Gym,-,"Kit; changing rooms close 12:25",Scheduled; 13:00-13:45,Lunch,-,-,-,-,Scheduled; 13:45,P5,French,Rm 9,Mme Dubois,-,Scheduled; 14:45-15:45,P6,Art,Studio,-,-,Scheduled

**Best at:** seeing the whole day and its status in one glance, from a distance. **Worst at:** warmth, and phones: seven columns get cramped on a small screen.

